# 26. Docker Containerisation

The Azure Functions application is containerised using Docker.

The project contains a:

```text
Dockerfile
```

The Dockerfile is used to build an image containing the CoffeeNChill Azure Functions application.

---

# 27. Build the Docker Image

From the project directory:

```powershell
docker build -t coffeenchill-functions:v1.0 .
```

Verify the image:

```powershell
docker images
```

The image should appear as:

```text
coffeenchill-functions
```

with the tag:

```text
v1.0
```

---

# 28. Run the Functions Container

The CoffeeNChill Functions image can be started using Docker.

Example:

```powershell
docker run -d `
  --name coffeenchill-functions `
  -p 7071:80 `
  coffeenchill-functions:v1.0
```

Check the container:

```powershell
docker ps
```

View the Functions container logs:

```powershell
docker logs coffeenchill-functions
```

